{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"ArcaniaBot","id":"810907841329627137","is_bot":1,"username":"ArcaniaBot"},"author_id":"810907841329627137","channel_id":"851552515345350657","content":"Unusually, the bells slowly toll twelve times, for the same time announcing midnight. Announcing an end of an era, and a beginning of another.\nBesides the loud ringing, that doesn't seem to disturb the sleep of anyone deep in their dreams, the city's mostly quiet.\nSure, there is the usual commotion around the Broadway, the fey are still running their carnival games, the lamplighters of Kingsbridge chat to one another while on the duty, and there is an occasional soul rifling through the rubble of Hampstead.\nBut after everything, finally, the city has a chance to unwind, and take a long-deserved rest.\n\nGood night, Empire City.\nHave a great new day, every day, from now on.","created_at":"2021-08-28T07:00:00.055000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"881070597965242429","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
